  "question": {
    "text": "Two satellites <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;are revolving around a planet in coplanar and concentric circular orbits of radii <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> respectively in the same sense. Their respective periods of revolution are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>hour</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>hours</mi></math> respectively. The radius of the orbit of A is equal to <math><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi></math>. What is their relative speed when they are closest?\r",
